{"success": true, "data": {"stdout": "{"text": "Given a signed 32-bit integer x, return x with its digits reversed. If reversing x causes the value to go outside the signed 32-bit integer range [-231, 231 - 1], then return 0.\n\nAssume the environment does not allow you to store 64-bit integers (signed or unsigned).\n\n \n\nExample 1:\n\nInput: x = 123\nOutput: 321\nExample 2:\n\nInput: x = -123\nOutput: -321\nExample 3:\n\nInput: x = 120\nOutput: 21\n\nSOLUTION : \nclass Solution:\n    def reverse(self, x: int) -> int:\n        if x >= -2**31 and x <= 2**31-1:\n            if x >= 0 :\n                result = int(str(x)[::-1])\n                if result >= -2**31 and result <= 2**31-1:\n                    return result\n                else :\n                    return 0\n            else :\n                result = int(('-'+str(x))[::-1])\n                if result >= -2**31 and result <= 2**31-1:\n                    return result\n                else :\n                    return 0\n        else :\n            return 0\n        \n      \nCOMPLEXITY : TC-O(N) and SC-O(N) where n is number of digits in x", "depth": 0, "seed_id": 118, "token_count": 512}
